  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, which builds the medieval handcart procedurally with Aura3D primitives. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run it in a browser, so none of it has been rendered or looked at.\n\n- **Bed:** 10 floor planks with slight variation in length, tone, tilt and height. Boards on all four sides and 2 cross rails per side. 4 corner posts with iron straps and bolts.\n- **Wheels:** 2 wheels on a shared axle. Each has a hub with iron bands and a cap, 12 spokes, wooden felloe segments and an iron tyre. That makes `spokeCount` 24.\n- **Frame and handles:** sills, cross beams and bearing blocks under the bed. 2 long rear push handles with grips and a tie bar. A front prop stand with 2 splayed legs and a foot bar.\n- **Cargo:** 3 sacks, 2 barrels with iron hoops and 2 stacked crates.\n- **Ground and lighting:** a dirt plane with 4 mounds and 16 scattered stones. The `golden-hour` look preset supplies the warm light, with soft PCF shadows.\n- **Camera and motion:** a fixed three-quarter camera. The whole cart turns slowly on a turntable while the wheels spin, driven from `app.onFrame`.\n- **Task state:** after `app.ready()` and two animation frames, it sets `window.__TASK_STATE__` to `{ ready: true, wheelCount: 2, spokeCount: 24, plankCount: 10 }` and `window.__EVAL_READY__` to `true`.\n\nThe riskiest guesses are the rotation conventions. If the wheels or handles look wrong, check the rotation signs on the wheel segments, the handle tilt and the prop legs. I also assumed the preset's sun and shadow overrides take effect as written.\n\n",
